n "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{2x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{2}\\int -\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167406 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166770 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6071303-6be5-5636-a675-66d33864a7c9" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using Arsech"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "596af3ac-2cfd-5fb7-ade3-485cc5e4e473" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525436} {:answer/id #uuid "ac5789dd-06d1-5697-9373-3b3a88db1cee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525642} {:answer/id #uuid "ba6f2c88-cb73-5051-96fd-18566c25f80a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525686} {:answer/id #uuid "bc6dd48c-9d36-5bf5-98a3-e7cf782bd81b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525690} {:answer/id #uuid "d5c09918-844e-5b3b-bab8-76822a18384d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525738}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc6dd48c-9d36-5bf5-98a3-e7cf782bd81b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525690} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f01b2e8-db8e-5abb-b7a2-af954c49c8a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fef2d4a0-63bd-50d5-be34-68f559ae65d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-95819" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{2(1-{x}^{2})}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "$$\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{2(1-{x}^{2})}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\int -\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526105 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166770 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6071303-6be5-5636-a675-66d33864a7c9" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using Arsech"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22e72ed6-10db-5dbf-8c92-fb49209d799a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{x/4}+\\operatorname{arsech}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525287} {:answer/id #uuid "706f7a64-b16d-5039-8c09-ef557473c94f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(2{e}^{x/4}-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525490} {:answer/id #uuid "8580ab23-a791-5de8-ad6b-0cc63fa0de49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{x/4}-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525542} {:answer/id #uuid "ec584e3e-8ce0-51c0-9c97-649c10128b3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(2{e}^{x/4}+\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525791} {:answer/id #uuid "f1278ff8-aa96-5223-9ec0-4bcb2bd5b37e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({e}^{x/4}-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "706f7a64-b16d-5039-8c09-ef557473c94f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(2{e}^{x/4}-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525490} :answer-field/id #uuid "15d3de90-b2df-5995-be5c-ba73c2ab86b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525856}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fdc2c42a-a78e-544f-8c57-a29a8369b036" :question/math-academy-id "q-95823" :question/problem "$\\int ({e}^{x/4}+\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}})\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "$$\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({e}^{x/4}+\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}})\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x/4}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{x/4}-2\\int -\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{e}^{x/4}-2\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x+C \\\\  & =2(2{e}^{x/4}-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526038 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166771 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c7d3082-d63a-5eac-9a9b-47681f8d4694" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using Arcoth"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ecb81a4-3878-5abc-9ce3-eae983c7585f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{8}\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525361} {:answer/id #uuid "4869ca01-d1e5-58e8-954c-d1bc23bcad5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{8}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525388} {:answer/id #uuid "53d8ae1d-ce5a-5d8e-a5d7-0f62cef54266" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525423} {:answer/id #uuid "93b0ea8f-d18b-5ec1-9b16-c9acb929650e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{8}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525581} {:answer/id #uuid "998e60e9-798f-50e1-b778-507e43e9329a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525598}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ecb81a4-3878-5abc-9ce3-eae983c7585f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{8}\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525361} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e499c8e-d040-53ca-a02f-43d6eaef1573" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "71d6f25e-3ed3-51ba-912e-8201182714bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-95829" :question/problem "$$\n\nCalculate $\\int -\\frac{7x}{8x-8{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x$ for $|x|>1.$" :question/worked-solution "$$\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int -\\frac{7x}{8x-8{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int -\\frac{7x}{8x(1-{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int -\\frac{7}{8(1-{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{8}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{8}\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
